From: djnice <djnice77@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AMLCodec: software 3D MVC decoding (edge264 + mvcout)

The S5 hardware MVC decoder corrupts the dependent view on some discs. With the
mvcout kernel module loaded and Kodi built with edge264-mvc, 3D MVC is decoded
on the CPU and both views are composed into one picture (frame packing at full
resolution, mono, or half resolution side-by-side / top-bottom) that goes to
the video layer through the amlvideo queue like a hardware decoder's frames.
Always used on S5, a setting on the other Amlogic SoCs.

With it:
- StereoscopicsManager: no notification loop when playing in mono.
- AMLDisplay: frame packing only on frame packed modes, a modeset when frame
  packing is entered or left (the mode name stays), 3D mode labels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
